// @run
// @log 3
// @log 5
// @log false
// @log 3
// @hint redundant type annotation: `inc` is inferred as `i32` — remove it to lean on inference
// @hint redundant type annotation: `big` is inferred as `boolean` — remove it to lean on inference
// @hint redundant type annotation: `half` is inferred as `f64` — remove it to lean on inference
// The three return annotations are kept DELIBERATELY (and their hints declared): the point
// of the file is the callback's SIGNATURE reaching the pin, so each one is spelled out.
// THE CASE THE `$fnsig` PIN'S PLACEHOLDER WAS SILENTLY WRONG FOR — and it was check-clean
// INVALID WASM, not a reject.
//
// A generic whose callback parameter is pinned by its `$fnsig` KEY (`=>ii>i`) records that
// key as the instance's parameter NAME. The key is a spelling the EMITTER minted for
// itself, so `nameToTy` cannot parse it back and `recordClonedNodeTyKnown` fell through to
// the placeholder `funcPinTyIx()` — a `TyFunc` with ZERO params and `fnRet = -1`.
//
// That placeholder is banked into `pinnedTyIx` and handed to `monoInferListElem`, which
// `declare`s it and RE-CHECKS the generic body to type the un-annotated `out`. Against a
// 0-param / -1-return function, `f(xs[i])` has no result type, so the inferred list never
// got an element type:
//
//   i32 / boolean callback -> `vl check --codegen` rc 0, `vl run`
//                             "type mismatch: expected i32, found (ref $type)"
//   f64 callback           -> `emitProgram: index access but list type not collected`
//
// The argument's real arena `TyFunc` was in hand at the call site the whole time; it is now
// handed over as a FALLBACK (`recordClonedNodeTyFb`) for exactly this pin.
//
// ANNOTATING the result hides it — `function mapAll<T>(xs: i32[], f: T): i32[]` runs
// correctly on master — which is why the corpus has 2,017 files and not one of them moves.
// The shape needs an INFERRED result list, and every corpus generic annotates one.
//
// `PIN_ANON` is NOT converted, and that is measured rather than conservative: the same
// hand-over for `#anonN` reddens five `tests/cases/inference/hole-*` chains, because
// `#anonN` names a specific INTERNED ROW rather than merely being unparseable. See
// `recordClonedNodeTyFb`.
function collect<T>(xs: i32[], f: T) {
  const out = []
  let i = 0
  while i < xs.length {
    out.push(f(xs[i]))
    i = i + 1
  }
  out
}

function inc(v: i32): i32 {
  v + 1
}

function big(v: i32): boolean {
  v > 9
}

function half(v: i32): f64 {
  v * 1.5
}

const a = collect([2, 4], inc)
print(a[0])
print(a[1])

const b = collect([2], big)
print(b[0])

const c = collect([2], half)
print(c[0])
